{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"760f640b2604d7651243e0270bb9761338e538b8fc726cc9dc572e8f5294427d","digest":{"component_or_area":"inbound fetcher / project mapping","key_entities":["fetcher.py","projects_store.py","apply_inbound_records.py","_build_snapshot","jqls_for","get_parent_map","get_comment_map","get_issuelinks_map","resolve_inbound_bridge_fields","_inbound_create_write_create_event","bridge_project","repos","_ACLI_CEILING","SilentTruncationError","projects_store.read_projects"],"problem_keywords":["multi-project inbound fetch","JQL fan-out","source project recording","enrichment passes","inbound ticket provenance"],"propositions":["The inbound fetcher currently processes only a single tracker project per store despite stores listing multiple projects in their mappings, silently dropping enrichment data for all but one project.","Inbound-created tickets do not record their source project, leaving bridge_project and repos fields unset.","The fetch operation must fan out JQL queries and all three enrichment passes (parent, comment, issuelink) once per configured project, merging results into a shared snapshot deduplicated by jira key.","The per-query truncation ceiling (_ACLI_CEILING) must apply independently per project rather than as a shared budget across all projects.","Inbound ticket creation must stamp bridge_project (derived from jira key prefix) and repos (from project mapping) fields via a new helper in projects_store."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787705376671420001,"uuid":"4ae94509-f2c9-4491-9828-d19a524891a4"}